# Files copied into each new `claude --worktree <name>` checkout.
#
# .gitignore syntax; only files that match here AND are git-ignored are
# copied. A worktree starts from tracked content only, so the committed
# safe-default env files (`.env.development`) already travel with it and the
# stack runs out of the box. List here only the git-ignored personal
# overrides a session would otherwise lose — they win over the committed
# defaults. Patterns without a slash match at any depth.
#
# NOT copied, intentionally: virtualenvs (they hardcode absolute paths, so a
# copy is broken) and node_modules (heavy; the package manager reinstalls
# fast from its store). Install inside the worktree when you need to build or
# test there.
#
# Never list a production secret file here — production secrets don't live
# in project repos at all (CLAUDE.md, "Secrets").
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
